[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. The reports in it describe three problems.
Each one has its own ticket in [paulochoi/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows-run2](https://github.com/paulochoi/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows-run2/issues).

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix does not close #4471 on its own. The booking-v3 hint and the one-day shift need their own fixes.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} repo="paulochoi/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows-run2" />

## What each problem is

- **Parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first. The shared parser reads the month first, so 7 April becomes 4 July. This is the bug #4471 names.
- **The booking-v3 hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`.** On booking-v3 tenants' forms, people type the month first, as the hint tells them. The form then reads the date day first. The parser plays no part, so its fix will not close this.
- **Dates are one day off or differ by time zone.** These reports describe a date that moves by one day, or a meeting that falls on different days in Lisbon and Toronto. Day and month are not swapped. The desk notes (`desk-notes.json`) mark them as a one-day move.

## How we counted

The export holds rows that overlap between pages, so reports are counted once by id. Causes come from `causes.ts`, using each report's tenant (locale and form) and channel. Intake's tag is a guess from the browser, and it often disagrees with the cause. The "tagged as" column shows how often. The desk's own table:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Outcome

Engineering update, #4471 closed 5 October:

- **parser**: fixed by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Ticket #1 closed as completed.
- **hint**: won't fix, because the booking-v3 form was retired. Ticket #2 closed as not planned.
- **one-day shift**: the update does not mention it. Ticket #3 stays open.

## Why one ticket hid three

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports by subject line. Reports with the same subject but different causes were merged into one ticket, and nobody read the bodies.

